WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
<b>This is a work of fiction. Persons, places, institutions,
and groups mentioned in the show have no relation
to actual persons, places, institutions, or groups.</b>

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:42.080
It's so nice and sunny.

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:46.770
Atmospheric pressure: 1003.9 hPa.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:49.270
Chance of rain: 0%.

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:53.590
A lot of people came to watch this year, too.

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:58.710
Spectator occupancy of home straight: 127%.

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:03.200
I wonder who will win this year.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:04.620
Unknown.

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:08.970
Well, it's nearly time.

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:10.710
Ai-chan, how do you feel?

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:12.360
Normal.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.770
I see. Shall we get started, then?

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:22.700
In five, four, three, two, one, cue.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:28.160
<i>Good morning, Miyakejima!</i>

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:35.240
Analysis Nene Itagaki                          Commentary Ai Makita

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:35.250
This season's Miyakejima Tourist Trophy, 
AKA the Miyakejima TT, has begun!

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:39.410
<i>I, Ai Makita of the Miyakejima Girls' 
High School Broadcasting Club,</i>

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:41.040
<i>will provide running commentary.</i>

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:45.220
<i>And I, Nene Itagaki, will 
be providing analysis.</i>

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:48.710
<i>We'll start today</i>

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:56.180
<b>Girls' High School Racing Kneeler National Tournament</b>

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:53.990
<i>with the Girls' High School Racing Kneeler
National Tournament exhibition race.</i>

00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:56.190
<i>How does it look out there, Itagaki-san?</i>

00:02:56.190 --> 00:03:01.250
This race is a demonstration 
for our fans to get to know

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:03.840
this season's drivers and passengers.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:08.440
<i>It may feel a bit lacking since 
there won't be any fierce battles,</i>

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:08.360
<i>Kanae Kawamata
Mao Katakura
Alisu Amano
Chiyuki Shiobara
Izumi Murata
Maria Shishido
Yuri Miyata</i>

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:08.360
<i>Tamae Kuribayashi
Hitomi Iseki
Kurosu Itou
Misaki Nagai
Nagisa Suzuki
Yuria Shishido
Megumi Meguro</i>

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:13.920
<i>but you can look forward to 
seeing that in the final round.</i>

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:16.880
<i>The skies are clear, and the wind is mild.</i>

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:20.310
<i>The fighting spirits of 
the ladies gathered from</i>

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:25.270
<i>all over the country here at Miyakejima, 
the Mecca of kneeler racing, are blazing!</i>

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:30.260
Now, let's introduce the racers 
aiming for victory this season!

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:37.760
Kazeno Tenpoint

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:38.720
<i>In the pole position are the "Bullet of Naniwa" 
from Osaka Ikoma Girls' High School,</i>

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:43.350
<i>driver Kanae Kawamata and 
passenger Tamae Kuribayashi!</i>

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:49.330
<i>Do you suppose they're wishing their 
dreams of victory will "come-ae true-ae?"</i>

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:52.370
What kind of lame joke 
was that? Yer slippin'!

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:53.370
It wasn't so bad.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:56.100
Besides, Kanae-chan, you let 
your tires slip all the time.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.150
You too, dummy!

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:05.330
Setsugekka

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:02.510
<i>In the second position 
are Hyogo Taka Academy's</i>

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:08.120
<i>cross-dressing beauty, driver Mao Takakura,
and passenger Hitomi Iseki!</i>

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:11.700
Since this is just the introductory 
race, let's take this one easy, Hitomi.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:13.940
That isn't like you, Mao.

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:16.900
I thought you aimed to win,
even when it's just for fun.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:20.330
Yeah, right. I'm not a child.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:27.560
Lovely Purgatory Slash

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:25.170
<i>In the third position are Kyoto Amagase</i>

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:29.430
<i>Girls' Academy's driver Alisu Amano 
and passenger Kurosu Itou!</i>

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:32.580
<i>They're supersonic goth-loli 
dolls and self racing queens,</i>

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:36.080
<i>but will they be able to 
achieve victory on the course?</i>

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:40.250
Let's paint the track our color, Kurosu.

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:42.250
Indeed, Alisu.

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:43.930
It will be glorious.

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:50.940
<i>In the fourth position are the princesses 
of Mie Suzuka Girls' Academy,</i>

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:55.210
<i>driver Chiyuki Shiobara and 
passenger Misaki Nagai!</i>

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:58.480
This is shaping up to be a wonderful race.

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:00.690
Don't you agree, Misaki?

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.450
We'll see.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:08.730
<i>In the fifth position are Ibaraki 
Tsukuba Girls' High School's</i>

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:11.270
<i>sadistic and dishonest driver Izumi Murata</i>

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:14.700
<i>and masochistic and dishonest 
passenger Nagisa Suzuki!</i>

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:18.380
I won't forgive you if 
you hold me back, Nagisa.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.710
I'll do my best, Izumi-san.

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:23.630
I don't care if you try.

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:25.800
We have to win. Got it?

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:28.150
Got it. I-I'll do my best.

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:33.380
<i>In the sixth position are 
the Motegi Twin Racers</i>

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:40.490
<i>of Tochigi Motegi Girls' High School, driver 
Maria Shishido and passenger Yuria Shishido!</i>

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:41.920
It's hot out.

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:44.630
It sure is. Our tires will soften quickly.

00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:48.180
They sure will. The grip 
will increase the G's.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:50.630
We'll be fine. Everyone's 
experiencing the same conditions.

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:57.900
Ashitabamaru

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:57.220
<i>Finally, in the rear are Tokyo 
Miyake Girls' High School's</i>

00:05:57.220 --> 00:06:01.250
<i>driver Yuri Miyata and 
passenger Megumi Meguro!</i>

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:06.140
<i>As Miyakejima's local team, 
they're favorites to win the race!</i>

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:12.340
Will Yuri-san and Megumi-san 
be okay, Wada-sensei?

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:14.640
They're acting like they always do.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:17.000
Does that mean they're not okay?

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:19.550
Nope. It couldn't be worse.

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:20.560
Yikes.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:21.900
Mutsuki-chan.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:24.270
I'm sure it'll work out.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:25.740
Right, Tsugumi?

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:27.860
Yeah, Hibari's right.

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:30.270
They're being their usual selves.

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:33.980
It's just a friendly race between warriors!

00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:36.580
They'll have to keep their savage spirits 
in check for this demonstration!

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:39.400
<i>It may be an exhibition race, 
but their irrepressible</i>

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:41.790
<i>fighting spirits are reaching 
the broadcast booth.</i>

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:44.580
<i>The riders are starting their engines!</i>

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:48.010
<i>The roar of their 600cc Supersport 
bikes rings across the track!</i>

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:49.930
<i>The red flag is leaving the track!</i>

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:53.470
<i>The starting signal is lighting up!</i>

00:06:56.870 --> 00:06:58.360
<i>They're all red!</i>

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:00.980
<i>And it's the blackout!</i>

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.690
No, no!

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:05.190
I'm gonna be late!

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:07.030
You're late, Megumi!

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:07.820
What are you doing?

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:09.400
So are you!

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:10.920
How long were you gonna sleep?

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:12.780
First period is modern Japanese!

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:14.460
Aw, nuts. That's Nakabayashi.

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:16.250
He'll hit us if we're late.

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:17.410
Step on it!

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:18.290
Of course!

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:43.830
Sounding great.

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:00.150
<b>Sidecar Club</b>

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:00.160
What?

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:02.670
You were late again?

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:04.390
It was Yuri's fault.

00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:06.940
She didn't take the right turn 
around Tairoike fast enough.

00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:09.550
It's because you didn't apply enough weight.

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:12.130
We would've understeered if I'd done that.

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:13.650
No, we wouldn't.

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:14.800
We would!

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:16.640
The other day I thought

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:19.320
we were gonna fly off the course 
and crash into the guardrail.

00:08:17.690 --> 00:08:20.730
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:08:21.280 --> 00:08:23.430
That's because you applied too much weight.

00:08:23.430 --> 00:08:25.500
See? We understeered.

00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:30.380
Is leaving five minutes earlier 
not an option for you two?

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:31.720
No way.

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:35.780
Even if I woke up early,
I'd just have to wait for Yuri.

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:37.090
What was that?

00:08:37.090 --> 00:08:38.910
You're the one who always makes me wait!

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:41.600
I only wait for you because I'm 
slower without a passenger!

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:43.910
Yeah, but it won't even run without a driver!

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:46.250
You have one! I'm always awake!

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:48.630
You two never change.

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:50.590
Wada-sensei.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:52.310
You two are exactly alike.

00:08:52.310 --> 00:08:54.470
It makes sense that you're 
so in tune with each other.

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:57.830
We're nothing alike.

00:08:57.830 --> 00:09:00.480
Yeah. Our appearances and 
tastes are totally different.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:02.220
Our personalities are opposite, too.

00:09:02.550 --> 00:09:05.850
That's not true. You two are pretty similar.

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:08.940
Your tastes are exactly the same, 
and you even do the same things.

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:10.650
Really?

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:11.800
Really.

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:14.360
Since you look visually different, 
it makes you seem all the more similar.

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:17.700
Well, we have been neighbors 
since we were kids.

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:21.060
And we grew up seeing and 
doing the same things.

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:24.430
I guess we like the same things...

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:32.470
As a special ward, this island 
has roads with no speed limits.

00:09:32.470 --> 00:09:36.730
So racers gather from all 
over to drive at full speed.

00:09:39.910 --> 00:09:43.890
Lots of racers move here so 
they can drive on the island.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:47.220
There are plenty of 
multi-generational racers, too.

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:54.030
When TT season rolls around, 
our inn is packed with guests.

00:09:54.430 --> 00:09:57.990
Since we were little, we grew 
up watching those people.

00:09:58.300 --> 00:10:01.560
At some point, we started wanting 
to race ourselves someday.

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:02.860
And then...

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:05.000
Coach Tanahashi!

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:09.210
Surpass all others to become the best.

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:10.580
Right?

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:11.380
Yes, sir!

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:15.460
They're alike, aren't they?

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:16.380
Yeah.

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:19.110
Get changed. We'll drive around the course.

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:20.140
Yes, sir!

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:33.860
<i>And they're off!</i>

00:10:35.590 --> 00:10:38.200
<i>And they're off!</i>

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:42.370
<i>The passengers are transferring their 
weight to the rear tire to gain traction!</i>

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:47.420
<i>The prelude to the Girls' High School Racing 
Kneeler National Tournament has begun.</i>

00:10:47.420 --> 00:10:52.790
The first riders to enter the corner 
are car number 22, Kazeno Tenpoint!

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:56.170
<i>Driver Kanae Kawamata's excellent 
cornering skills are supported</i>

00:10:56.170 --> 00:11:00.380
<i>by passenger Tamae Kuribayashi's 
precise weight control!</i>

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:04.240
<i>The engine they've tuned with their superb 
skills seems to be in top condition, as well!</i>

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:08.670
Gaze upon the glory of 
our finely tuned engine!

00:11:08.670 --> 00:11:10.610
Kanae-chan, you're on fire.

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:12.860
It's just an exhibition race. 
You don't need to try so hard.

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:15.570
I won't let anyone ride in front of us.

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:18.090
Don't do anything crazy!

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:20.200
We've still got the rest 
of the track to cover!

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:24.510
<i>Behind them are car number 44, Setsugekka!</i>

00:11:24.510 --> 00:11:26.740
<i>Mao Katakura's clean steering and</i>

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:30.830
<i>Hitomi Iseki's beautiful positioning 
resonate like a tuning fork!</i>

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:33.540
Un, deux, trois.

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:35.260
En dehors!

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:38.990
Un, deux, trois.

00:11:39.600 --> 00:11:40.720
En dedans!

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:44.800
They're so fast.

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:46.940
They're all strong schools.

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:48.750
Can we even win?

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:51.650
I'm not sure that's the problem.

00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:53.190
Right.

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:56.600
But they're good as long as they're riding.

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:57.760
<b><i>Yuri Miyata</i></b>

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:57.760
<b><i>Megumi Meguro</i></b>

00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:57.850
I know.

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:06.530
<i>Left turn into downhill coming up.</i>

00:12:06.530 --> 00:12:09.040
<i>I'll turn-in early for 
a deeper clipping point.</i>

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.500
<i>There's the traction.</i>

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:13.190
<i>Full speed ahead.</i>

00:12:14.430 --> 00:12:15.710
<i>Amazing.</i>

00:12:15.990 --> 00:12:18.950
<i>He knows all the lines I want to take.</i>

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:21.140
<i>Right uphill turn coming up.</i>

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:22.700
<i>We'll shift our weight forward and—</i>

00:12:30.260 --> 00:12:31.140
Here they come.

00:12:33.130 --> 00:12:34.670
Goal!

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:42.200
Welcome back.

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:43.280
Thanks.

00:12:45.690 --> 00:12:46.530
How was our time?

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:48.300
Incredible.

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:49.790
That was two seconds faster.

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:52.150
This is only the beginning.

00:12:53.090 --> 00:12:54.680
You'll get even faster.

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:56.330
Really?

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:57.180
Yeah.

00:12:57.590 --> 00:12:59.660
You could even break my course record.

00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:02.940
Your light weight gives you an advantage.

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:07.080
Only if we're as good as you, Coach.

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:08.760
I'll teach you the skills.

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:10.910
Miyata, switch with me.

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:12.780
Meguro, you're the passenger.

00:13:12.780 --> 00:13:13.500
Got it.

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:16.730
<b>Miyake Girls' High School</b>

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:24.820
<i>Straightaway ahead.</i>

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:26.340
<i>Left turn ahead.</i>

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:28.490
<i>Right downhill turn ahead.</i>

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:30.460
<i>No! We're losing time!</i>

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:33.830
<i>He went deep into the turn</i>

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:35.860
<i>and used his front brakes to cover for me?</i>

00:13:36.260 --> 00:13:37.540
<i>He...</i>

00:13:37.910 --> 00:13:40.190
<i>understands me...</i>

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:48.740
<i>He understands me.</i>

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:56.620
<i>Currently in third is car number 66,</i>

00:13:56.620 --> 00:14:00.510
<i>Lovely Purgatory Slash, team 
Alisu Amano and Kurosu Itou!</i>

00:14:00.510 --> 00:14:02.570
<i>They're slowly catching up to second!</i>

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:06.030
We won't hold back just 'cause 
it's an exhibition race.

00:14:06.310 --> 00:14:08.780
If anything, we'll stand out!

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:12.410
<i>What's this? Kurosu Itou 
boldly takes the inside!</i>

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:15.090
Lovely Purgatory Slash 
is going for the inside!

00:14:15.090 --> 00:14:18.420
They're keeping their grip 
by preventing a roll.

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:20.750
Not bad.

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:25.050
What? We didn't discuss this!

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:28.180
You think I'd be satisfied 
with a well-mannered plan?

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:31.390
<i>Lightning Tornade is 
boldly attacking, as well!</i>

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:33.710
<b><i>Yuri Miyata</i></b>

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:33.710
<b><i>Megumi Meguro</i></b>

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:33.720
<i>Bringing up the rear is Ashitabamaru!</i>

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:38.530
We've fallen really far behind.

00:14:38.530 --> 00:14:39.630
How's our time?

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:41.430
Ten seconds behind first.

00:14:41.430 --> 00:14:42.760
We're still dead last.

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:44.150
Don't worry.

00:14:45.060 --> 00:14:46.600
That's still within range.

00:14:46.600 --> 00:14:48.650
They can bring it back.

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:53.050
I hope you're right, but they're 
being their usual selves, right?

00:14:53.050 --> 00:14:55.300
Yup, their usual selves.

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:57.060
It couldn't be worse.

00:15:17.050 --> 00:15:18.020
It's done.

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:21.020
Yeah. This is our bike.

00:15:21.340 --> 00:15:22.750
The dimensions of the body...

00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:25.110
Its tendencies while driving...

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:27.870
They're all perfectly customized for us.

00:15:28.250 --> 00:15:29.590
We should name it.

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:30.390
Yeah.

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:33.280
How about "Ashitabamaru?"

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:35.260
Coach Tanahashi.

00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:40.960
When the Ashitaba's leaves are torn, 
they grow back by the next day.

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:42.540
This island's known for them.

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:45.500
No matter how difficult things 
get, you always get back up.

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:48.210
It's the perfect name for you.

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:49.310
Yes, sir.

00:15:50.400 --> 00:15:52.180
No matter what hardships you encounter,

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:54.640
<b>Ashitabamaru</b>

00:15:53.070 --> 00:15:54.640
<i>always get back up.</i>

00:15:56.810 --> 00:16:02.480
In fifth is car number 33, the Alsvid's 
team Izumi Murata and Nagisa Suzuki!

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:05.690
<i>They're closing the gap 
with their wild riding!</i>

00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:10.090
The G's!

00:16:10.090 --> 00:16:11.030
Slow, aren't you?

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:12.210
<i>What's this?</i>

00:16:12.210 --> 00:16:14.070
<i>They're taking the corner 
with one tire in the air!</i>

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:16.560
<i>The Alsvid is attacking by reducing 
the resistance of its tires!</i>

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:19.550
But it's a double-edged sword that can 
reduce your grip by puncturing the tire.

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:20.900
It's a high-level technique.

00:16:20.900 --> 00:16:24.210
In sixth is car number 55, Single Duet's team

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:26.790
<i>Maria Shishido and Yuria Shishido!</i>

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:28.630
<i>No matter how you look at it, 
they're one and the same!</i>

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:33.130
<i>The twin racers ride as one!
The self-doppelgangers have arrived!</i>

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:34.980
Ashitabamaru is maintaining its speed.

00:16:34.980 --> 00:16:36.560
Are they waiting to see what'll happen?

00:16:36.990 --> 00:16:39.720
<b>Sidecar Club</b>

00:16:37.810 --> 00:16:39.380
The coach is quitting?

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:43.480
He's quitting at the end of the 
month and moving to England.

00:16:43.770 --> 00:16:45.000
England?

00:16:45.470 --> 00:16:46.940
You mean...

00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:48.900
That's right. The Isle of Man.

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:50.390
The Isle of Man?

00:16:50.390 --> 00:16:51.740
Then...

00:16:52.090 --> 00:16:53.750
The Isle of Man TT.

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:57.560
It's a long-established race that's 
been held for over a hundred years.

00:16:57.560 --> 00:17:00.330
Kneelers across the world 
dream of racing there.

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:03.550
Most of the top racers are 
residents of the Isle of Man.

00:17:03.550 --> 00:17:05.670
Open your front door, and 
the track's right there.

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:09.130
They enter the race knowing 
every gap in the road's surface.

00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:13.060
The best way to win at the 
Isle of Man is to live there.

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:15.960
But this is too sudden.

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:17.640
Why are you doing this?

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:19.390
Because of you two.

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:24.650
You learned everything I had to 
teach you and improved your skills.

00:17:25.110 --> 00:17:27.270
At first you were slow, but you've grown

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:31.000
to the point that you're nearly 
breaking my course record.

00:17:31.330 --> 00:17:35.400
Seeing that made me realize 
I can't sit here forever.

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:39.990
I'll win the Isle of Man TT.

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:42.530
What about the sidecar club?

00:17:42.530 --> 00:17:45.960
You said you'd help us win 
the national tournament!

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:49.170
<b>Ashitabamaru</b>

00:17:46.310 --> 00:17:48.770
It'll be fine. You can do it.

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:51.460
I've taught you everything I can.

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:53.210
Now it's up to you.

00:17:53.870 --> 00:17:57.220
I'll win in the world I've set my sights on.

00:17:57.220 --> 00:18:00.870
You win in yours.

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:08.030
<i>Last place bike Ashitabamaru is accelerating!</i>

00:18:08.030 --> 00:18:09.860
<i>Yuri-chan and Megumi-chan 
are making their move.</i>

00:18:09.860 --> 00:18:11.840
<i>They're passing Single Duet!</i>

00:18:11.840 --> 00:18:13.250
<i>They did it.</i>

00:18:15.460 --> 00:18:17.200
Ashitabamaru? They're fast.

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:18.320
Izumi-san!

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:19.450
We've still got this.

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:21.240
No way!

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:24.890
<i>Ashitabamaru has climbed to fifth!</i>

00:18:24.890 --> 00:18:28.870
<i>Will Yuri Miyata and Megumi 
Meguro race to victory?</i>

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:29.610
<b><i>Yuri Miyata</i></b>

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:29.610
<b><i>Megumi Meguro</i></b>

00:18:31.180 --> 00:18:32.710
<i>Dear Coach Tanahashi.</i>

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:36.920
<i>There's something I want to 
tell you before you leave.</i>

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:41.270
<i>Please come to Maigoji at 
Tairoike after school today.</i>

00:18:41.860 --> 00:18:43.200
<i>Please.</i>

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:46.180
<i>Yuri Miyata.</i>

00:18:46.550 --> 00:18:47.760
<i>Megumi Meguro.</i>

00:18:54.590 --> 00:18:58.080
<i>Ashitabamaru has caught up 
to Lovely Purgatory Slash!</i>

00:18:58.080 --> 00:19:00.050
<i>This isn't a friendly 
exhibition race anymore!</i>

00:19:00.050 --> 00:19:02.490
<i>This is turning into a heroic battle!</i>

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:07.000
Megumi, what's wrong?

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:09.710
Huh? Oh, nothing.

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:12.770
What about you? What are you doing here?

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:15.670
Nothing, really.

00:19:19.350 --> 00:19:21.900
Yuri, what about tomorrow's exam?

00:19:21.900 --> 00:19:24.170
Shouldn't you be studying?

00:19:24.170 --> 00:19:25.660
I'll be fine.

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:29.520
But shouldn't you head 
home so you can study?

00:19:29.880 --> 00:19:32.480
I've already given up.

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:33.970
That's no good!

00:19:33.970 --> 00:19:35.970
You should definitely go home!

00:19:35.970 --> 00:19:38.190
I'm saying this for your sake!

00:19:38.430 --> 00:19:40.280
Well, shouldn't you be helping your family?

00:19:40.850 --> 00:19:42.830
My mom's taking care of it!

00:19:42.830 --> 00:19:48.500
No, your inn gets lots of guests 
who look forward to your cooking!

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:50.290
You should go home and help!

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:53.630
I'm saying this for your sake!

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:56.290
Well, your family runs an inn, too!

00:19:56.290 --> 00:19:57.770
You should go home!

00:19:57.770 --> 00:19:59.270
No, you!

00:19:59.270 --> 00:20:00.520
No, you!

00:20:00.520 --> 00:20:01.440
Thanks for waiting.

00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:04.510
You're both here?

00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:07.500
What did you want to talk about?

00:20:07.500 --> 00:20:08.250
Huh?

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:14.590
<i>Ashitabamaru is locked in a 
fierce battle with Setsugekka!</i>

00:20:14.590 --> 00:20:16.260
<i>Neither one's giving any ground!</i>

00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:18.780
<i>It's a battle for their honor!</i>

00:20:19.680 --> 00:20:21.490
What is it? What's wrong?

00:20:23.870 --> 00:20:25.210
Um, I—

00:20:32.200 --> 00:20:34.510
Good luck at the Isle of Man TT!

00:20:32.200 --> 00:20:34.510
I'll be rooting for you, Coach!

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:39.590
We'll win the national tournament, too!

00:20:39.900 --> 00:20:42.340
So, good luck!

00:20:42.710 --> 00:20:44.780
Yeah, you, too.

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:48.350
Achieve victory in your world.

00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:50.940
<i>Ashitabamaru is battling its final opponent!</i>

00:20:50.940 --> 00:20:53.980
<i>They're challenging their opponent head-on!</i>

00:20:57.100 --> 00:20:57.990
<i>I'll...</i>

00:20:58.640 --> 00:20:59.560
<i>I'll...</i>

00:21:00.520 --> 00:21:01.860
I'll win in

00:21:03.440 --> 00:21:04.820
my world!

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:10.750
<i>Ashitabamaru wins!</i>

00:21:10.750 --> 00:21:13.210
<i>They've boldly taken first place!</i>

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:16.460
That was an intense battle, Itagaki-san.

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:17.420
It was.

00:21:17.770 --> 00:21:21.050
<i>They showed passion despite 
this being an exhibition race.</i>

00:21:18.690 --> 00:21:22.630
<i>Yuri Miyata
Kanae Kawamata
Mao Katakura
Alisu Amano
Chiyuki Shiobara
Izumi Murata
Maria Shishido</i>

00:21:18.690 --> 00:21:22.630
<i>Megumi Meguro
Tamae Kuribayashi
Hitomi Iseki
Kurosu Itou
Misaki Nagai
Nagisa Suzuki
Yuria Shishido</i>

00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:23.500
<i>I'm looking forward to the finals now.</i>

00:21:24.360 --> 00:21:28.610
<i>The second and third place teams 
are commending their partners.</i>

00:21:29.350 --> 00:21:32.230
<i>The winners Yuri Miyata 
and Megumi Meguro are</i>

00:21:32.230 --> 00:21:36.250
<i>also looking at each other as if to 
confirm how the other is feeling.</i>

00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:42.650
<i>They're about to share their 
passionate spirit with one another!</i>

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:45.860
<i>No, wait! They hit each other!</i>

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:47.430
It's a cross-counter!

00:21:47.430 --> 00:21:49.490
What a beautiful hit!

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:51.240
<i>They've both fallen, and neither is moving!</i>

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:53.200
<i>Is this a double-knockout?</i>

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:53.200
One! Two!

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:55.790
They were alike until the very end.

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:54.780
Three!

00:21:55.350 --> 00:21:56.180
Four!

00:21:55.790 --> 00:21:59.920
It went as badly as we thought it would.

00:21:56.650 --> 00:21:57.580
Five!

00:21:57.970 --> 00:21:58.840
Six!

00:21:59.360 --> 00:22:00.480
Seven!

00:22:00.820 --> 00:22:03.800
Eight! Nine!

00:22:04.340 --> 00:22:06.360
Ten!
